{"id": "86251", "name": "שני ישרים במשוואה אחת – נקודת החיתוך (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>The following equation represents two straight lines. Determine the point of intersection of these two lines:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} . \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\([ x,\\, y ]\\) = [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Factor the quadratic expression into two linear factors: each factor equal to zero is one of the lines. The intersection point solves the system of the two linear equations.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The two lines</b><br>The quadratic equation can be factorised as (expand to check)<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ ({{CT:1}})({{CT:2}}) = 0, \\]</p>and a product is zero exactly when one of the factors is zero. So the two lines are \\({{CT:3}}\\) and \\({{CT:4}}\\), and we need to find the solution of the system<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:3}}, \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:4}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Solving the system</b><br>Subtracting the second equation from the first eliminates \\(x\\):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:5}}=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y={{CT:6}} \\]</p>Substituting this into the first equation:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ x+{{CT:7}}\\cdot\\left({{CT:6}}\\right){{CT:8}}=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x={{CT:9}} \\]</p>This gives<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ [x,y] = {{CT:10}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 10, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "rank", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 2, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "correctanswer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["Y86251", "correctanswer", "eq1", "eq2", "n1", "n2", "n3", "n4", "p", "sol", "wronganswer"], "nvariants": 50}